=== a typo in an index or TTL expression suggests the column
--- ALTER TABLE t ADD INDEX i ix TYPE minmax GRANULARITY 1
Code: 47. Unknown expression identifier `ix`. Maybe you meant: ['id']. In scope ix. (UNKNOWN_IDENTIFIER)
--- ALTER TABLE t MODIFY TTL ix + INTERVAL 1 DAY
Code: 47. Missing columns: 'ix' while processing: 'ix + toIntervalDay(1)', required columns: 'ix', maybe you meant: 'id'. (UNKNOWN_IDENTIFIER)

=== a name that is nothing like a column still gets the list of available columns
--- ALTER TABLE t MODIFY TTL zzzzzzzzzzzz + INTERVAL 1 DAY
Code: 47. Missing columns: 'zzzzzzzzzzzz' while processing: 'zzzzzzzzzzzz + toIntervalDay(1)', required columns: 'zzzzzzzzzzzz', available columns: 'tp' 's' 'd' 'x' 'id'. (UNKNOWN_IDENTIFIER)

=== an expression added to the sorting key may use only the columns added by the same ALTER, so only they are suggested
--- ALTER TABLE t ADD COLUMN idx UInt32, MODIFY ORDER BY (id, idz)
Code: 47. Unknown expression identifier `idz`. Maybe you meant: ['idx']. In scope id, idz. (UNKNOWN_IDENTIFIER)
--- ALTER TABLE t ADD COLUMN n UInt32, MODIFY ORDER BY (id, idz)
Code: 47. Unknown expression identifier `idz`. In scope id, idz. (UNKNOWN_IDENTIFIER)
--- ALTER TABLE t MODIFY ORDER BY (id, idz)
Code: 47. Unknown expression identifier `idz`. In scope id, idz. (UNKNOWN_IDENTIFIER)
--- ALTER TABLE t MODIFY ORDER BY (id, _part_indez)
Code: 47. Unknown expression identifier `_part_indez`. In scope id, _part_indez. (UNKNOWN_IDENTIFIER)

=== a subcolumn is legal in a key, so it is suggested too
--- ALTER TABLE t ADD COLUMN tp2 Tuple(a UInt32, b String), MODIFY ORDER BY (id, tp2.c)
Code: 47. Unknown expression identifier `tp2.c`. Maybe you meant: ['tp2.b','tp2.a']. In scope id, tp2.c. (UNKNOWN_IDENTIFIER)
--- CREATE TABLE t2 (id UInt32, tp Tuple(a UInt32, b String)) ENGINE = MergeTree ORDER BY (id, tp.c)
Code: 47. Unknown expression identifier `tp.c`. Maybe you meant: ['tp.b']. In scope id, tp.c. (UNKNOWN_IDENTIFIER)

=== the same expressions, spelled correctly
id, idx, tp2.a
